            "paragraph": "Diffusion models, a more recent class of generative tech- niques, have also shown promise for producing realistic, high-fidelity climate fields with controllable stochasticity. Mardani et al. (2025) introduced a Corrective Diffusion (CorrDiff) framework that combines a deterministic UNet regression with a stochastic diffusion model to downscale 25 km reanalysis data to 2 km resolution over Taiwan, achieving physically realistic enhancements in coherent structures such as typhoons and frontal systems, as well as synthesizing radar reflectivity.",
