            "target_entity_instance": "Beijing",
            "target_entity_type": "City",
            "paragraph": "Most recently, Zou et al. (2024) applied an MPS-based spatial downscaling frame- work to refine coarse-resolution precipitation fields from the CMORPH satellite precipitation product using the CMPAS 1-km, hourly rainfall dataset from the China Meteorologi- cal Administration, which merges radar, gauge and satel- lite data, as TIs. In a case study over Beijing, the method preserved mean areal rainfall magnitudes while accurately reproducing storm spatial structure and return-level pat- terns. To illustrate how the approach operates in practice, Fig. 1 compares the original coarse-resolution CMORPH rainfall field with the corresponding MPS-derived 1-km fields. The left panels show the reference CMORPH pre- cipitation at 8-km resolution, including a zoomed-in view of the subregion of interest, while the right panels display the downscaled fields before and after the intensity-adjust- ment step. This visual comparison highlights the ability of MPS to reconstruct fine-scale storm structure and localized extremes that are absent in the coarse satellite product.",
